I mean, everybody I know watched it.


00:44:04.100 --> 00:44:05.300
You know, if NBC went by


00:44:05.300 --> 00:44:07.600
Blackwater's ratings alone,
we'd be on forever.


00:44:15.400 --> 00:44:17.400
Doggone it! You gotta tuck it in there...


00:44:26.400 --> 00:44:27.700
Break!


00:44:27.800 --> 00:44:28.900
Amy.


00:44:29.000 --> 00:44:30.200
There you are.


00:44:30.300 --> 00:44:31.500
- Hey. Sorry.
- Hello.


00:44:31.600 --> 00:44:32.900
Ran into the girls.


00:44:33.000 --> 00:44:34.300
This is Janice.


00:44:34.400 --> 00:44:35.500
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:44:35.600 --> 00:44:36.700
I ran into you in town,


00:44:36.700 --> 00:44:38.300
- didn't I, at Blackie's?
- Yeah.


00:44:38.300 --> 00:44:39.800
You'll probably see me
hanging around there,


00:44:39.900 --> 00:44:41.700
'cause my daddy's always hanging out there.


00:44:41.800 --> 00:44:43.600
- Who's your father?
- Tom Heddon.


00:44:43.600 --> 00:44:45.900
You know, he used to be coach, years ago.


00:44:46.000 --> 00:44:47.600
A very memorable man.


00:44:47.600 --> 00:44:49.300
Yeah.


00:44:54.900 --> 00:44:57.500
So, what are we all talking about?


00:44:57.600 --> 00:44:59.200
We are just giving shit to Amy 'cause


00:44:59.300 --> 00:45:01.500
she ain't been down here
to see us since she got here.


00:45:01.600 --> 00:45:03.400
Guess she don't want to be
hounded for autographs.


00:45:03.400 --> 00:45:05.100
Well, I was telling Kristen here


00:45:05.200 --> 00:45:07.400
that we've been very busy
fixing up the house and all.


00:45:07.400 --> 00:45:09.100
Amy's been busting her butt
up there while I work,


00:45:09.200 --> 00:45:10.500
- so I can vouch for that.
- That's right.


00:45:10.600 --> 00:45:12.700
- Hey, y'all.
- Well, hey, handsome.


00:45:12.800 --> 00:45:14.400
May I?


00:45:16.700 --> 00:45:17.900
Hello, buddy.


00:45:18.100 --> 00:45:19.300
He ain't moving about today, is he?


00:45:19.400 --> 00:45:21.300
Yeah, taking a nap, I suppose.


00:45:22.400 --> 00:45:24.300
How do you like our local music?


00:45:24.400 --> 00:45:26.600
It ain't quite your Beethoven.


00:45:26.700 --> 00:45:28.100
Hey, man, go on and knock up somebody


00:45:28.200 --> 00:45:30.600
your damn self. This here's mine.


00:45:30.700 --> 00:45:33.200
See there, Mr. Sumner,
you ain't the only one with a trophy wife.


00:45:33.300 --> 00:45:34.500
Only difference is


00:45:34.600 --> 00:45:36.000
mine's for third place.


00:45:36.300 --> 00:45:37.600
Believe it or not,


00:45:37.600 --> 00:45:39.500
that's the most romantic
thing he's ever said.


00:45:39.800 --> 00:45:41.900
That and, "You're what?"


00:45:44.200 --> 00:45:45.800
Hello, Amy.


00:45:45.900 --> 00:45:47.300
Hello, Jeremy.


00:45:47.400 --> 00:45:48.800
How are you?


00:45:48.900 --> 00:45:50.200
- Hello, Janice.
- Get out of here.


00:45:50.200 --> 00:45:51.400
Hi.


00:45:51.500 --> 00:45:53.000
Niles, why don't you go over there
and watch practice.


00:45:53.100 --> 00:45:55.200
Jeremy, you need to get, okay?


00:45:55.300 --> 00:45:57.100
- Goddamn, boy!
- Jesus, Daddy!


00:45:57.200 --> 00:45:58.500
Kick the shit out of you!


00:45:58.600 --> 00:46:00.500
- You fucking...
- Daddy, no!


00:46:02.500 --> 00:46:03.900
- Come on!
- Stop it, Coach!


00:46:04.000 --> 00:46:05.500
- Jesus, Coach!
- All right, Coach.


00:46:05.500 --> 00:46:07.000
Get off me!


00:46:07.000 --> 00:46:08.100
Hey, Coach, come on, that's enough!


00:46:08.200 --> 00:46:10.000
- Daddy!
- I didn't do anything.


00:46:10.100 --> 00:46:12.200
- Stop it, Coach.
- Daddy, stop!


00:46:15.000 --> 00:46:17.000
Come on, son.


00:46:17.100 --> 00:46:19.100
Get up.


00:46:19.200 --> 00:46:21.200
All right. All right.


00:46:22.000 --> 00:46:23.100
Attaboy.


00:46:23.200 --> 00:46:26.700
Listen... I do not want
to hurt you, Jeremy Niles.


00:46:26.800 --> 00:46:28.600
I am just protecting my family.


00:46:28.700 --> 00:46:30.600
All right?


00:46:30.700 --> 00:46:31.900
But Janice is my girlfriend.


00:46:32.000 --> 00:46:34.400
- God damn it!
- Daddy! Somebody stop him!


00:46:34.500 --> 00:46:35.900
You understand me?


00:46:36.000 --> 00:46:37.300
- Right on, Coach!
- Do you?


00:46:37.400 --> 00:46:39.300
- You stop it, Coach! Enough.
- Or what? You're gone, Amy.


00:46:39.400 --> 00:46:41.200
- Hey!
- Enough.


00:46:41.200 --> 00:46:42.500
- You don't even live here any more.
- All right.


00:46:42.600 --> 00:46:43.800
- Hey.
- That's enough.


00:46:43.900 --> 00:46:45.600
- You ain't got no right.
- That's enough, that's enough.


00:46:45.700 --> 00:46:46.900
- Let's go.
- No right to be involved.


00:46:47.000 --> 00:46:48.200
- He was just talking, Coach.
- Amy...


00:46:48.300 --> 00:46:50.000
Mr. Sumner, think that's a very good idea.


00:46:50.100 --> 00:46:51.700
- Just walk away.
- He was just talking.


00:46:51.800 --> 00:46:53.300
You got no right to be involved, Hollywood.


00:46:53.300 --> 00:46:55.600
Neither do you. He was just talking.


00:46:55.600 --> 00:46:57.000
Jeremy, Jeremy.


00:46:57.100 --> 00:46:58.900
Hey, hey, hey... Eyes... Come on, let's go.


00:47:00.500 --> 00:47:02.600
Amy. Hey.


00:47:03.500 --> 00:47:04.800
- Hey!
- What?


00:47:04.900 --> 00:47:06.800
- I'm not very happy with you.
- Oh, no?


00:47:06.900 --> 00:47:08.600
Why'd you have to
throw yourself into that, huh?


00:47:08.700 --> 00:47:10.700
With that drunk? Are you crazy?


00:47:10.700 --> 00:47:11.900
Somebody had to do something.


00:47:11.900 --> 00:47:13.200
- Somebody had to?
- Yes.


00:47:13.300 --> 00:47:14.500
What does that mean?


00:47:16.600 --> 00:47:17.700
Look at me.


00:47:17.800 --> 00:47:19.000
I'm talking to you.


00:47:20.700 --> 00:47:22.500
I'm not gonna get in the fucking fray.


00:47:22.600 --> 00:47:25.500
I don't care if it's how
things are done here.


00:47:25.500 --> 00:47:26.600
Against my principles.


00:47:29.500 --> 00:47:32.700
It's awfully convenient, your principles.

